592186059155 #edb/ref 1080 "If it is not raining, then you cannot play in the garden." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059155 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059155 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9614552a-fb14-5c45-b7bc-b7a13a4686d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059156 #edb/ref 1080 "If you can play in the garden, then it is raining." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059156 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059156 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b084c643-6545-54d5-8a04-7b29662bc8e7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059157 #edb/ref 1080 "If it is raining, then you cannot play in the garden." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059157 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059157 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e1ba66d4-1d73-5a29-bd53-a9ab3ac3beb4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059158 #edb/ref 1080 "If you cannot play in the garden, then it is raining." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059158 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059158 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1a73bac2-a45a-5188-b000-3f140035bf97" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059159 #edb/ref 1080 "If it is not raining, then you can play in the garden." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059159 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059159 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4c52c90e-2a2c-541e-8c27-b3150dcbade7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059412 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12710" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059412 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the inverse of the following statement: \n\n$\\qquad$ **If** it is summer, **then** it is not snowy outside." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059412 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "144f352c-5696-5ad3-841f-3a6a1cf2e5f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059412 #edb/ref 1074 "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A{:}$ It is summer.\n\n- The consequent is $B{:}$ It is not snowy outside.\n\nThe inverse of a conditional statement $A \\Rightarrow B$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\neg A \\Rightarrow \\neg B.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B{:}$\n\n- $\\neg A{:}$ It is not summer.\n\n- $\\neg B{:}$ It is snowy outside.\n\nTherefore, the inverse is the following: \n\n$\\qquad$ If it is not summer, then it is snowy outside." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059413 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12711" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059413 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the converse of the following statement:\n\n$\\qquad$ **If** it is summer, **then** it is not snowy outside." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059413 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9f3fe8eb-f539-539e-96c6-33b6a238fc82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059413 #edb/ref 1074 "In our conditional statement:\n\n- The antecedent is $A{:}$ It is summer.\n\n- The consequent is $B{:}$ It is not snowy outside.\n\nThe converse of a conditional statement $A \\Rightarrow B$ is given by \n\n$$\nB \\Rightarrow A.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the converse is the following: \n\n$\\qquad$ If it is not snowy outside, then it is summer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059414 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12712" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059414 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the contrapositive of the following statement: \n\n$\\qquad$ **If** it is summer, **then** it is not snowy outside." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059414 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9e1fa00b-8e51-5689-959d-049df21077bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059414 #edb/ref 1074 "In our conditional statement: \n\n- The antecedent is $A{:}$ It is summer.\n\n- The consequent is $B{:}$ It is not snowy outside.\n\nThe contrapositive of a conditional statement $A \\Rightarrow B$ is given by \n\n$$\n\\neg B \\Rightarrow \\neg A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the negations of $A$ and $B{:}$\n\n- $\\neg A{:}$ It is not summer.\n\n- $\\neg B{:}$ It is snowy outside.\n\nTherefore, the contrapositive is the following: \n\n$\\qquad$ If it is snowy outside, then it is not summer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059415 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12713" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059415 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\qquad$ **If** it is summer, **then** it is not snowy outside.\n\nWhich of the following statements are equivalent to the conditional statement above?\n\n- If it is not summer, then it is snowy outside.\n\n- If it is not snowy outside, then it is summer.\n\n- If it is snowy outside, then it is not summer." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059415 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "31e2f48c-65cc-53c3-b34c-70e2c53a9274" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059415 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's recall the following facts:\n\n- The contrapositive is logically equivalent to the original statement.\n\n- The inverse and the converse are logically equivalent to each other, but not to the original statement.\n\n![](images/d9/d946d2a81d46cbde934ebbab54f9b69b514092e02da4f8a3b79768f218929449.png)\n\nSo, we are looking for the contrapositive of the given statement.\n\n- Statement I is the inverse, not the contrapositive. $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n- Statement II is the converse, not the contrapositive. $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n- Statement III is the contrapositive. $\\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059691 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050360 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060111 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186060422 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186378313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186379288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186380207 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059691 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186404211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059691 #edb/ref 1039 "Finding the Converse of a Statement" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186059691 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186059413 #edb/ref 